      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bartlett earned its name when founder Luther Bartlett donated half of his 40‑acre woodlot and money to build the 1873 train depot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bartlett%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village still preserves its original 1873 railroad station, a relic that once linked dairy farmers to Chicago.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bartlett%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "German immigrants flocked to Bartlett after the depot opened, turning the area into a bustling hub of factories, stores, and saloons.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.bartlettil.gov/about-bartlett/village-of-bartlett-museums/history-of-bartlett",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The old Set‑Screw factory beside the tracks was once Huntley Dairy, a landmark that stood until very recently.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.bartlettil.gov/about-bartlett/village-of-bartlett-museums/history-of-bartlett",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Bartlett Historical Society curates local artifacts in The Quiet Room, offering a glimpse into the town’s rich past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.bartlettlibrary.org/learn-discover/genealogy-local-history",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
